Hogwarts Legacy, and their respective titles, characters, names, settings and
translations.

"Source Content" means all material owned by the rights holders of the Source
Works or by other third parties.

"Original Contribution" means material in the Work authored by the licensor or
contributors, excluding Source Content and Third-Party Components.

"Third-Party Components" means material licensed by others, which remains under
its own license.

"Derivative Work" means any work based on the Work, such as modifications,
adaptations, translations, ports, conversions to other formats, forks,
extensions or integrations.

"Output" means text or other material generated by an AI model while a person
plays with, or otherwise runs, the Work.

"Corresponding Source" means the preferred form of the work for making
modifications: the human-readable text, Markdown, JSON and scripts as
distributed, including any scripts needed to convert or build the other formats.
Obfuscation, encryption, "hidden definition" settings, packing or locking of
prompt text or code in a way that prevents recipients from reading and reusing
it as permitted by this License is not permitted.

"Commercial Use" means any use primarily intended for commercial advantage or
monetary compensation, directly or indirectly, including but not limited to:
  a) Selling, licensing, renting or sublicensing the Work or Derivative Works
     for a fee.
  b) Placing the Work, Derivative Works, updates, early access, or any feature
     of them behind a paywall, membership, subscription, donation tier, or
     "supporter-only" gate (e.g. Patreon, Afdian/愛發電, Ko-fi, Boosty, Gumroad,
     paid card or lorebook marketplaces, or similar).
  c) Bundling or distributing the Work with paid or ad-supported products,
     services, apps, bots or hardware.
  d) Monetized distribution: ad-shorteners, pay-to-download, "key" or survey
     walls, ad-funded download pages, or crypto/token gating.
  e) Use within a company, or for a client, as part of a for-profit activity,
     including paid commissions to write or adapt prompts, cards or lorebooks.
  f) Using the Work to train, fine-tune or evaluate a model, or to build a
     dataset, for a paid product or service, or as input to a paid product or
     service that redistributes its functionality.


